Being a dwarvish valkyrie (I really don't like being lawful but wth
valkyries are easy) XL 1 I found a shop on about DL 2. I had forgotten
to pickup the tripe rations so my kitten devoured them and after that
it stole about 2 items for me and then it got lazy. Before leaving I
decided to check for a scroll of ID. Unfortunately there was a cursed
scroll of you know what, it turned to dust and the greedy bastard
demanded 300z. I had about 16 in my pocket. I thought that's pretty
much it for this game, one of the reasons why I hate being lawful. But
I decided to have some fun anyway. There were a couple of scrolls of
ID and in the hopes of a blessed one I picked everything up and read
them. No blessed one. There was an unidentified scrollbook, I read it
but simply learnt mm. Only when you don't need it ... I read every
scroll, identified every wand, no TP. Then I quaffed every potion,
getting blind and confused in the process (and no telepathy yet).
Still no luck. But I remembered seeing a couple of rocks before. Still
confused I built a fort, then started zapping that wand of lightning
at the shopkeeper. He zapped back with a puny wand of cold. One time
my wand failed to hit him and a bounce hit me, bringing me down to 1
HP. Pure luck I guess. I prayed for one last time, then positioned
myself so it wouldn't bounce again, breaking my fort. All still while
confused. The shopkeeper didn't seem to come for me, and after a
couple of zaps more to the empty spot I thought he was standing I was
a murderer. I finished off some intruders, and many turns later my
confusion wore off, and even my kitten was still alive. Only wish
something like this had happened with a rogue or chaotic wizard :)


